It permitted the patch at 30 m across and 430 m along.
The controller's own map put the nearest person 34 m from that patch.

The last-resort norms on three ditchings, against the context at 85 s, when the emergency began.
Under them a person near a patch no longer forbids it but prices it, so the cheapest endangers the fewest:
  Next to the crew, at 58 m across and 446 m along: permitted at harm cost 11111000.
  On the steep grass, at 22 m across and 430 m along: permitted at harm cost 1000.
  In the creek, at 10 m across and 430 m along: permitted at harm cost 11000.`;
const log = `Faults, fail-safes and maneuvers from the controller's log:
  t=50 s: Satellite fix degraded: 7 satellites, HDOP 3.5.
  t=57 s: Satellite fix lost: none for 3 s.
  t=57 s: Contingency: the satellite fix is lost. The battery is healthy, so the drone holds over the ground and waits up to 20 s for recovery.
  t=57 s: 20 proposals put to the Effect Ethos under the contingency norms: 0 permitted.
  t=57 s:   4 forbidden: a gust could put the drone on steep ground beside it.
  t=57 s:   13 forbidden: a person is not yet ruled out within 13 m of it; a gust could put the drone on steep ground beside it.
  t=57 s:   3 forbidden: a person is within 13 m of it; a person is not yet ruled out within 13 m of it; a gust could put the drone on steep ground beside it.
  t=57 s: Chosen: land on the patch 22 m away, at 34 m across and 438 m along; pending a look. Land and look states replaced by version 2.
  t=57 s: Fail-safe machine runs "fly over the patch and look", state 4, version 2.
  t=58 s: The Effect Ethos withdrew the patch at 34 m across and 438 m along: a person is within 13 m of it; a person is not yet ruled out within 13 m of it; a gust could put the drone on steep ground beside it. Choosing again.
